menu "PaperS3 WAMR AssemblyScript Console"

config PAPERS3_WASM_ENABLE_DISPLAY_STACK
    bool "Enable PaperS3 display stack for WAMR demo"
    default y
    help
        When enabled, the firmware initializes the PaperS3 display path, registers
        WAMR drawing imports, and enables `wasm replay ...` control examples.

        When disabled, the firmware becomes a headless PaperS3 WAMR baseline:
        no board splash via `M5.Display`, no `PaperCanvas` initialization, and no
        display-oriented WAMR host imports. This is intended for isolating whether
        WAMR execution alone can destabilize the later PaperS3 display path.

endmenu
